module



@[expose] public section
/-!
# MONO kernel checker v2 (core Lean only; soundness in `MonoSound.lean`)

Data for one leading exponent: `kμ` (its key), `n` (row count), `N` (packed rows, 64-bit slots
`w = s + 2^6·(v1 + 2^5·(v2 + 2^5·v3)) + 2^21·c`, variable code 31 = absent): the rows mean `c · x_{v1} x_{v2} x_{v3} · t_s`.
`key x = Σ x_i 8^i`. `checkV d kμ n N` = every slot valid (s < 48, codes < 24 or = 31, multiplier degree d − 2) and the
key-sorted mod-P accumulation of the expansion (zero entries dropped) has head key `kμ`.
All recursion is through explicit recursors (`List.rec`/`Nat.rec`) and Bool `bif` on GMP-accelerated `Nat.blt/beq`,
which measured ≈ 3× faster in the kernel than `match`/`if` definitions.
-/
namespace MonoKV

abbrev P : Nat := 1048573

/-- the 48 trinomials (BookQuadricDictionary.terms renamed to grevlex positions): `(a, b, e)`, `a ≤ b`, `e ∈ {1, P-1}` -/
